00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:07.200
@darawkay4021
Do you have any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.560
plans to make videos similar to&nbsp;
"Life of a Hanseatic Merchant"?

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:18.120
Ok, let me tell you, I had lots of problems&nbsp;
with that video. When you’re doing a life of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:23.880
an X kind of person in history, there’s a lot of&nbsp;
historical nuance that gets lost and there’s also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:39.660
usually a lot of guesswork that’s being made.&nbsp;
This is mainly because our sources are varied,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:44.760
they are a combination of many things, from&nbsp;
official histories, to surviving inscriptions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:48.660
to administrative documents, to&nbsp;
mentions in third party writings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:54.060
etc. This varied and limited nature of the&nbsp;
sources, especially for classical and middle ages,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.060 --> 00:02:00.000
naturally often paints an incomplete picture which&nbsp;
then doesn’t translate well into trying to present&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:06.360
a complete life of a historical character kind&nbsp;
of story. There’s just too many unknowns. For&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:12.300
example, all the hazing information we have about&nbsp;
the Bergen Contor comes from outsiders laughing at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:17.760
how ridiculous it is. Therefore, we don’t have a&nbsp;
complete picture of it, nor do we know the hazing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:23.880
I described was something recurring or it just&nbsp;
happened to be the type of hazing they did that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:28.800
specific year that we have the source from. We&nbsp;
have other sources from different times mentioning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:34.560
there was hazing but we don’t know if the hazing&nbsp;
was always the same. Not to mention that as I say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:39.600
in the video the life of a Hanseatic merchant&nbsp;
changed over time as the league existed for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:45.660
hundreds of years and trying to present a coherent&nbsp;
single story from just one decade is impossible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:52.020
because a lot of the surviving sources span a&nbsp;
century. The sources describing the recruitment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:57.900
might have been from 1404 while the surviving&nbsp;
administrative documents might have been from 1491&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:04.620
while the hazing source could have been from 1444,&nbsp;
etc. A lot can happen in a hundred years and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:09.540
therefore, after I finished that video I kind of&nbsp;
realized that presenting this story of the life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:16.020
of an “average” 14th century Hanseatic merchant is&nbsp;
misleading. Not to mention that even if we find a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:21.240
diary of a Hanseatic merchant from that time whose&nbsp;
to say his story was the quote unquote “average”.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:27.900
These kinds of “life of an X” stories are just&nbsp;
often misleading and present a sort of uniformity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:33.180
in past people’s lives that just didn’t exist.
I still published the video because I think it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:38.040
good and funny and I do emphasize the nuances&nbsp;
about the fact that a lot of people could have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:42.900
had a very different experience as merchants in&nbsp;
the Hanseatic league compared to what I presented,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:48.120
and nothing I said in the video was made up,&nbsp;
it’s still all in the sources, but doing such a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:54.660
video I think loses the context of the sources and&nbsp;
historical nuance and therefore I am reluctant to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:58.860
do another video like that. This doesn’t mean you&nbsp;
cannot make a good video in this sort of style,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:03.660
but it has to be a topic where we have&nbsp;
far more sources surviving, especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:09.720
personal sources like diaries. So I guess in&nbsp;
a long winded way my answer is, probably not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:15.583
and if yes it would be about something far better&nbsp;
documented than the life of a hanseatic merchant.

