00:07:59.811 --> 00:08:01.500
@DG-jp8yw
Do you know people who go to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:06.300
Oxford and Cambridge? What sort of occupations are&nbsp;
they doing now that there isn’t a colonial empire?

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:12.060
Hehe, good question. For those that don’t&nbsp;
get this go watch my Oxford and Empire video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:18.060
also for those that don’t know I went to Oxford&nbsp;
and now I am doing a PhD at Cambridge. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:23.280
Oxbridge, that is Oxford and Cambridge together,&nbsp;
are very much modern Universities at this point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:28.860
They underwent quite sizeable restructuring in the&nbsp;
latter half of the 20th century as the empire fell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:34.080
apart, for example, they began to higher a lot&nbsp;
more professors from all around the world not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:38.640
just from the Empire and they also opened up&nbsp;
the application process to basically anyone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:43.260
and they started a lot of outreach programs&nbsp;
which are necessary to help people from less&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:47.280
privileged backgrounds to even understand the&nbsp;
application process because the application&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:51.540
process to Oxbridge is a bit weird. During&nbsp;
this time also all the colleges in Oxbridge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:55.680
finally started to allow women to&nbsp;
get degrees, which, sidenote here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.680 --> 00:09:03.960
the history of women at Oxbridge is fascinating.&nbsp;
The bullshit they had to deal with for hundreds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:09.480
of years and the arguments they had to withstand&nbsp;
from grumpy old men were just the most ridiculous.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:13.860
There’s a book about it if you want to know&nbsp;
more. Anyways, due to all these changes and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:19.080
getting rid of legacy admissions which many high&nbsp;
end universities in America still have, Oxbridge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:24.240
is quite diverse these days and due to the breadth&nbsp;
of the intake of people from all around the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:29.400
the students here are truly some of the smartest&nbsp;
people in their field and they end up doing all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:34.080
kinds of jobs after they graduate. But if you&nbsp;
really want to know specifics Oxbridge releases&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:41.340
all the statistics on where their alumni end up.&nbsp;
Between 2012 and 2017 most Oxford alumni ended up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:47.040
in Academia and Higher Education, but that’s&nbsp;
only 15% with the rest being quite diverse.

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:47.403
